WEBVTT

00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:06.643
Every staff change now leaves a record: who made it, what it was, which record it

00:00:06.643 --> 00:00:07.975
changed, and when.

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:14.553
Starting a staff session is the first change on the books. When the code is right,

00:00:14.553 --> 00:00:18.518
one audit entry is written, with the time from the server's clock.

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:24.639
Signing out is audited too. The staff member is read before the session ends.

00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:32.768
A wrong password, a wrong code, or a sign-in left halfway records nothing.

00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:41.156
Behind it is one step in the command pipeline. A staff command carries a marker, its

00:00:41.156 --> 00:00:46.367
handler names the person and the record, and the change is saved with its entry.

00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:52.684
Forget to name the record, and the command fails, so nothing changes unaudited.

00:00:56.000 --> 00:01:01.166
The entry keeps identifiers only. No name, no email, no field values.

00:01:04.000 --> 00:01:08.108
Telemetry hears the action's name, and never who, or which record.

00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:14.922
Every test failed first. Now they all pass.

00:01:18.000 --> 00:01:20.600
Next, creating an event joins the trail.

00:01:24.000 --> 00:01:28.756
That's slice twenty-nine point two. Christian Fitness: a Christian community for

00:01:28.756 --> 00:01:30.602
health in body and spirit.
